    "shared-p": {
      "id": "shared-p",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Profiles change navigation and authoring choices, not the stored document. Shared ownership keeps blocks, references, identity, lints, and writing rules consistent across corpora. A profile therefore configures what an author sees and where content belongs without forking the block model. A document can move between conventions without conversion, and tools can reason about its blocks before they know the corpus subject. Profile-owned interview scripts can ask subject-specific questions while producing the same document objects and reference spans."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
